Linear Regression with OLS (Ordinary Least Squares) is a method used to find the best-fit line between the input features (X) and the target (Y).

The best-fit line is chosen by minimizing the sum of squared errors (residuals) between the actual and predicted values.

The regression equation is:

yf^=β0+β1x

β0= intercept
β1= slope (coefficient)

OLS finds the values of β0 and β1
	​
that make the prediction errors as small as possible.

